# Nexus frontend work

Source of truth: [`docs/frontend-standards.md`](docs/frontend-standards.md) and [`docs/frontend-patterns.md`](docs/frontend-patterns.md)

Applies to any of these frontend roots:

- `Nexus.Dashboard/` — current production dashboard
- `Refactor/web/` — refactor frontend
- `web/` — future post-refactor frontend root

Before changing UI, UX, layout, or React code in those trees, read and obey the frontend docs.

## Non-negotiables

- Use only the existing shadcn-style primitives in `src/components/ui/`
- Do not introduce a second UI kit or competing visual language
- Prefer the existing shell/layout/list/detail patterns before inventing new scaffolds
- Use revealing UI: primary path first, advanced detail on interaction
- Complex data must be structured (table, tabs, KPI strip, detail route), not dumped as raw JSON/text
- Do not ship god pages or god components; split by job, section, or route depth
- Show explicit loading, empty, success, and error states
- Prefer canonical examples from the active frontend root: `DashboardLayout`, `ListPageLayout`, `DataTable`, `AdminOperationsPage`, `AdminPaymentsPage`, `ScriptsCommandCenterPage`, `ScriptStudioPage`
- Homogeneous collections must use dense `DataTable` + filters + pagination — never card/button stacks as the primary list (see `docs/frontend-patterns.md` §2.1.1)
